      {
        "id": 14928,
        "name": "The Burning Stickman",
        "username": "The_Burning_Stickman",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_burning_stickman/{size}/2003_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-03-31T16:10:57.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>It's fairly common in comic books for some otherwise good, or at least non-villainous, person or group to start creating countermeasures in the event a hero or group of heroes goes rogue. Especially since Iron Legacy painted a pretty clear picture of that happening, I have to think that the Sentinels world is the same.</p><p>So, who out there -- excluding villains -- has been putting together plans to deal with the Freedom Five or others should they become a threat?</p><p>Revo Corp seems likely, as would the military at Ft. Adamant, to have something up their sleeve along these lines.</p><p>And what about other heroes? Does The Wraith, for instance, have a sample of the Regression Serum in case Paul snaps?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:47:09.290Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 10,
        "reads": 1,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 50.2,
