      {
        "id": 170225,
        "name": "hstein3",
        "username": "hstein3",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/hstein3/{size}/2159_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-04-01T14:59:25.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Heh, this was actually part of the plot I used when I ran a Sentinels RPG. (Not&nbsp;<em>the</em> RPG, <a href=\"http://mrhalbert.blogspot.com/2016/02/sentinels-of-multiverse-rpg-fate-edition.html\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">but mine</a>.) FILTER, which rebranded as SERUM (Superhuman/Extraterrestrial Response and Urgent Measures) after the Freedom Five decided they didn't want to be tied to the US government anymore, played the role of the \"human\" counter-response to superhumans. They had a number of ongoing projects:</p><ol>\n<li>Create an army of clones based on the gene-bound soldiers left behind by Voss in the aftermath of his invasion. An additional program (though further behind) involved&nbsp;<span>clones based on super-powered individuals that could be programmed to have unwavering loyalty to SERUM.</span>\n</li>\n<li>Integrate tech captured from the Omnitron robot with the Ironclad Project.</li>\n<li>Develop a superior super-serum based by integrating the progression serum and the Pike labs Barzakh formulas.&nbsp;</li>\n</ol><p>I'll admit now that I borrowed rather extensively from the first season of <em>Young Justice</em> to write my story, but I think it still made sense in the Sentinel universe.</p>",
        "post_number": 3,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:52:40.313Z",
