        "read": false,
        "user_title": null,
        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>Heh, this was actually part of the plot I used when I ran a Sentinels RPG. (Not&nbsp;<em>the</em> RPG, <a href=\"http://mrhalbert.blogspot.com/2016/02/sentinels-of-multiverse-rpg-fate-edition.html\">but mine</a>.) FILTER, which rebranded as SERUM (Superhuman/Extraterrestrial Response and Urgent Measures) after the Freedom Five decided they didn&#39;t want to be tied to the US government anymore, played the role of the &quot;human&quot; counter-response to superhumans. They had a number of ongoing projects:</p><ol><li>Create an army of clones based on the gene-bound soldiers left behind by Voss in the aftermath of his invasion. An additional program (though further behind) involved&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">clones based on super-powered individuals that could be programmed to have unwavering loyalty to SERUM.</span></li><li>Integrate tech captured from the Omnitron robot with the Ironclad Project.</li><li>Develop a superior super-serum based by integrating the progression serum and the Pike labs Barzakh formulas.&nbsp;</li></ol><p>I&#39;ll admit now that I borrowed rather extensively from the first season of <em>Young Justice</em> to write my story, but I think it still made sense in the Sentinel universe.</p>",
